(6) The total sign face area of a wall sign shall not exceed 20 percent of the total area of the wall on which it is painted or affixed; if in a shopping center, 20 percent of the wall area of each business. The area of the lower slope of a gambrel or mansard roof shall be counted as wall area when the sign is mounted on the lower slope of such roofs;
(7) Twenty-five feet on all streets where permitted within the county. On multilane divided highways, 30 feet where permitted within the county. In all residential zoning districts, six feet;
(8) The zoning administrator shall determine the minimum ground clearance required in consideration of setbacks, motorist visibility, pedestrian safety and all other pertinent factors. Unless otherwise required by these regulations or the zoning administrator, the minimum ground clearance shall be six feet, except in residential zoning districts;
(9) Signs shall be installed with a three foot setback from a property line, vertical or horizontal, provided:
a. No part of the sign overhangs the property line.
b. No part of the sign is within eight feet of electric power lines, vertical or horizontal of the conductors.
c. Wall, swinging or projecting wall signs mounted to the wall of buildings in the CG zoning district may overhang the right-of-way provided all other provisions of swinging or projecting wall signs are met.
(Res. of 6-6-02; Res. of 8-27-13)
