574:
Political signs shall be allowed without permits within any zoning district of the county subject to the following restrictions:
(1) A political sign or any structure intended solely for the support of a political sign shall not be erected more than 60 days prior to the election which the sign is intended to influence and shall be removed within ten days after the final election, including any runoffs, which the sign is intended to influence.
(2) No more than one political sign (which may be double-faced) per road frontage per candidate may be placed on any one premises.
(3) All political signs shall be supported by independent means and shall not be attached to any utility pole, to any street sign or any sign directing or controlling traffic nor to any pole or post supporting such signs, nor any trees, shrub or plant.
(4) The following type political signs or devices are prohibited:
a. Roof signs;
b. Sidewalk, and A-frame signs;
c. Portable signs;
d. Signs involving motion, sound or flashing lights;
e. Lighted signs;
f. Trailer signs;
g. Search lights or similar devices.
(5) The following type advertising devices intended to attract attention for political purposes are prohibited except when used at political rallies, parades or similar events but in no case shall such devices be displayed for longer than 24 hours:
a. Air- or gas-filled devices;
b. Balloons or streamers;
c. Flags or banners.
(6) No political signs shall be permitted on any public right-of-way.
(7) Political signs must be set back a minimum of ten feet from the curb or ditch centerline of any street and in no case shall the view of motorists or pedestrians be obstructed.
(8) No temporary political sign may exceed 16 square feet in area nor shall signs exceed ten feet in height. Minimum clearance between the bottom of the sign and the ground shall be six feet, yard signs excepted.
(9) Yard signs:
a. Yard signs are defined as signs not exceeding six square feet in area.
b. A permit is not required for yard signs.
c. No more than one yard sign (which may be double faced) per road frontage per candidate may be placed on any one premises.
d. Yard signs must be set back a minimum of ten feet from any street, and in no case shall the view of motorists or pedestrians be obstructed.
(10) Violation of the provisions of this section shall be punishable as provided in section 73-26.
(Res. of 6-6-02; Res. of 9-30-04; Res. of 8-27-13)
